ction","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UnknownAaguidAction","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What to do with an AAGUID that has no MDS entry (i.e. FIDO Alliance has no metadata for it —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not necessarily malicious, MDS coverage is incomplete for some legitimate authenticators)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/unknownaaguidaction","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnknownAaguidAction","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/PolicyResponse":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET"},{"type":"text","text":" response: the stored policy plus the unknown-AAGUID action it currently "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resolves to"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unknown_aaguid"},{"type":"text","text":" is nullable, where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" means “use this mode’s default” (deny under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direct_required"},{"type":"text","text":", allow otherwise). A client that only saw the stored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" would have to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-derive that rule itself to display what the policy actually does — and a security rule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implemented twice is a security rule that will eventually disagree with itself. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server resolves it once, here, and reports both: the admin’s stored intent and its effect."}],"title":"PolicyResponse","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/policyresponse","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentat